# FACoP code ownership.
#
# This file is the ESCALATION path, not the default path. Ordinary contributions are meant to
# be accepted autonomously by tools/facop-review on the strength of their proofs, with no
# maintainer reading them (docs/security-model.md §4).
#
# What cannot work that way is a change to the controls themselves: a PR that adds a key to
# the trust root, or edits a gate, could otherwise mint its own acceptance and every later
# forgery would verify correctly. Those paths — and only those — require a human. The list
# below mirrors the protected set in tools/facop-review/src/policy.zig; the two must agree.

# NOTE: there is deliberately no `*` default owner. A catch-all would force human review on
# every contribution and defeat the point of autonomous acceptance.

# --- Trust root ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Whoever merges a change here can add a producer whose signed evidence is accepted as
# honest. This is the single most security-sensitive file in the repository.
/config/trusted-keys.json           @suissa
/config/reference-attestation-key.pem @suissa

# --- The gates themselves --------------------------------------------------------------
# A change to a gate can disable the gate. Reviewing these is reviewing the enforcement.
/scripts/attest-lib.ts              @suissa
/scripts/attest.ts                  @suissa
/scripts/verify-attestation.ts      @suissa
/scripts/secret-scan.ts             @suissa
/scripts/workflow-guard.ts          @suissa
/scripts/qualify.ts                 @suissa
/scripts/evidence-key-lib.ts        @suissa
/scripts/hooks/                     @suissa

# --- The acceptance verifier -----------------------------------------------------------
# The program that decides acceptance must never be able to self-accept a change to itself.
/tools/facop-review/                @suissa

# --- Trust-plane definition ------------------------------------------------------------
# Workflow files decide what runs with which credentials.
/.github/workflows/                 @suissa
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @suissa

# --- Normative specification -----------------------------------------------------------
/docs/security-model.md             @suissa
/docs/spec/                         @suissa

# --- Upstream-owned acceptance evidence ------------------------------------------------
# CONTRIBUTING.md: contributor-authored changes here cannot serve as independent proof of
# the same patch without policy approval.
/tests/                             @suissa
/config/validation.yml              @suissa
